THOUGHT: `priority` is nullable and cleared to null, but `getPriority()` returns it directly with a non-null return type, causing the NullAway RETURN_NULLABLE error. The pattern used in `getDiskCacheStrategy()` is to return a default when the field is null. I’ll mirror that by returning a sensible default (e.g., `Priority.NORMAL`) when `priority` is null. Then I should run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '113,115c\  Priority getPriority() {
    if (priority == null) {
      return Priority.NORMAL;
    }
    return priority;
  }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/DecodeHelper.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

